<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seven Years' War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1756">1756</a>–<a href="/years/1763">1763</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Seven Years' War was a global conflict fought from 1756 to 1763 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and their allies and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and their allies. Fighting took place in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1763">Treaty of Paris</a> of 1763 transferred most of France's North American and Indian holdings to Britain, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a> profiles note.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seven-years-war.jpg" alt="Seven Years' War" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Blaue Max · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seven_Years%27_War_Collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
